{
  "$comment": [
    "GENERATED by tools/genref.java --items from a running a1.1.2 client jar.",
    "Do not edit by hand -- regenerate instead. Every column but `name` was read",
    "or measured out of the jar; see that tool's emitItems for how, and for why",
    "`places` is measured by using each item in a real world rather than read.",
    "`sheet` is which image the icon indexes: RenderItem picks terrain.png for",
    "ids below 256 and gui/items.png above, so the column is that rule applied.",
    "`places` is the block id the item puts down, or 0 for one that places none.",
    "`armour` is ItemArmor.armorType -- 0 helmet, 1 chestplate, 2 leggings,",
    "3 boots -- and -1 for everything that is not armour. It is the field",
    "SlotArmor.isItemValid compares against, so it is the game's own answer to",
    "which of the four slots a piece goes in rather than a reading of its name.",
    "`bucket` is ItemBucket.isFull: 0 for the empty bucket, the flowing block id",
    "for a full one (8 and 10, not the still 9 and 11), -1 for milk, and -2 for",
    "everything that is not a bucket at all.",
    "`damageVsEntity` is Item.getDamageVsEntity(null), the number",
    "attackTargetEntityWithCurrentItem passes to attackEntityFrom: 1 for",
    "everything that is neither a tool nor a sword, and a constructed field",
    "on the two classes that are. Null is safe -- no override reads the",
    "entity -- which is why it can be a column at all.",
    "`tills` is whether the item is an ItemHoe, asked as a class: a hoe",
    "writes farmland into the struck cell rather than into the face's",
    "offset, so `places` measures 0 for all five and cannot tell them from",
    "an item that does nothing.",
    "`fx` is 1 for an item whose icon tile a TextureFX rewrites every tick --",
    "the compass, and nothing else in this version. It is read off the FX",
    "class rather than matched by name; see emitItems.",
    "`spawns` is the entity this item puts into the world instead of a block:",
    "painting, boat, minecart or arrow, and `none` for everything else. It is",
    "why four items measure `places` as 0 and still do something. `spawnVariant`",
    "is ItemMinecart's own type field -- 0 cart, 1 chest, 2 furnace.",
    "`palette` is whether the Creative hand offers it: everything this version",
    "defines except an ItemBlock whose block already has a carried form, and a",
    "handful of engine-only ids named in emitItems."
  ],
